# Somnibeat

**Research prototype · not a diagnostic tool.**

Somnibeat turns one night of heartbeat intervals (an RR-interval CSV) into an
overnight sleep report: total sleep time, sleep efficiency, wake bouts and
suspected sleep-apnea minutes. Every estimate is shown next to how far this
kind of estimate differs from a hospital sleep study, measured on recordings
the models never saw during training.

- **Live demo:** https://handue.github.io/somnibeat/ (a static page; the file you load is analysed in your browser and never uploaded)
- **Written description:** [`docs/WRITEUP.md`](docs/WRITEUP.md)
- **Results:** [`results/`](results/) (every number in this README and in the demo is read from these files)

## What it does

| Output | How it is computed |
|---|---|
| Total sleep time, sleep efficiency, wake bouts | 30-second epochs classified sleep vs wake by gradient boosting on heart-rate-variability features |
| Suspected apnea minutes | 60-second windows classified by a separate gradient-boosting model |
| Wake / NREM / REM and wake / light / deep / REM (experimental) | Same features, multi-class models |

Each output sits next to two baselines: (a) asleep from lights-off, and (b) the
majority class of the training data.

## Headline results (external test: UCDDB, {{v:sleep_wake/data/test/ucddb/records}} overnight recordings)

Primary model: gradient boosting (chosen by internal cross-validation before
the test set was scored). Errors are model minus polysomnography; brackets are
record-level bootstrap 95% confidence intervals.

| Metric | Gradient boosting | Logistic regression | Asleep from lights-off |
|---|---|---|---|
| Total sleep time, mean absolute error (min) | {{pm:sleep_wake/models/gradient_boosting/external_ucddb/metrics/tst_mae_min:1}} | {{pm:sleep_wake/models/logistic_regression/external_ucddb/metrics/tst_mae_min:1}} | {{p:sleep_wake/baselines/asleep_from_lights_off/metrics/tst_mae_min:1}} |
| Total sleep time, bias (min) | {{sgn:sleep_wake/models/gradient_boosting/external_ucddb/metrics/tst_bias_min:1}} | {{sgn:sleep_wake/models/logistic_regression/external_ucddb/metrics/tst_bias_min:1}} | {{sgn:sleep_wake/baselines/asleep_from_lights_off/metrics/tst_bias_min:1}} |
| Sleep efficiency, mean absolute error (pct. points) | {{pm:sleep_wake/models/gradient_boosting/external_ucddb/metrics/se_mae_pctpt:1}} | {{pm:sleep_wake/models/logistic_regression/external_ucddb/metrics/se_mae_pctpt:1}} | {{p:sleep_wake/baselines/asleep_from_lights_off/metrics/se_mae_pctpt:1}} |
| Sleep/wake epoch kappa | {{pm:sleep_wake/models/gradient_boosting/external_ucddb/metrics/kappa_pooled:2}} | {{pm:sleep_wake/models/logistic_regression/external_ucddb/metrics/kappa_pooled:2}} | {{p:sleep_wake/baselines/asleep_from_lights_off/metrics/kappa_pooled:2}} |
| Apnea minutes, mean absolute error (min) | {{pm:apnea/models/gradient_boosting/external_ucddb/metrics/apnea_min_mae:1}} | {{pm:apnea/models/logistic_regression/external_ucddb/metrics/apnea_min_mae:1}} | {{p:apnea/baselines/no_apnea/metrics/apnea_min_mae:1}} (no apnea) |
| 3-stage kappa (experimental) | {{pm:wake_nrem_rem/models/gradient_boosting/external_ucddb/metrics/kappa_pooled:2}} | {{pm:wake_nrem_rem/models/logistic_regression/external_ucddb/metrics/kappa_pooled:2}} | {{p:wake_nrem_rem/baselines/asleep_from_lights_off/metrics/kappa_pooled:2}} |
| 4-stage kappa (experimental) | {{pm:four_class/models/gradient_boosting/external_ucddb/metrics/kappa_pooled:2}} | {{pm:four_class/models/logistic_regression/external_ucddb/metrics/kappa_pooled:2}} | {{p:four_class/baselines/asleep_from_lights_off/metrics/kappa_pooled:2}} |

Read these with the limitations in mind: the test set is small and made of
sleep-clinic patients, per-night errors are wide (Bland-Altman limits of
agreement for total sleep time: {{v:sleep_wake/models/gradient_boosting/external_ucddb/bland_altman/tst_min/loa_low:0}} to
{{v:sleep_wake/models/gradient_boosting/external_ucddb/bland_altman/tst_min/loa_high:0}} min), and logistic regression did better than the
primary model on this test set, which we report rather than switch models
after seeing test results. Full discussion in [`docs/WRITEUP.md`](docs/WRITEUP.md).

## Run the demo locally

The demo is plain HTML, CSS and JavaScript modules in `web/`; there is no build step.

```bash
python3 -m http.server 8000 --directory web
```

Then open http://localhost:8000/. Load one of the three sample nights, or
upload your own RR CSV:

```csv
time_s,rr_ms
1.4105,1113.22
2.5204,1109.95
```

`time_s` is the time of each beat in seconds since the recording started and
`rr_ms` is the interval ending at that beat. At least 2 hours of beats are
needed. Optional clock inputs (recording start, lights off, lights on) limit
the analysis to time in bed.

## Reproduce every number

Requirements (tested versions): Python 3.14, Node.js 24 (for the
Python/JavaScript parity tests), GNU or BSD `make`, about 25 GB of free disk for the raw
PhysioNet files, and an internet connection. No accounts are needed.

```bash
git clone https://github.com/handue/somnibeat.git
cd somnibeat
make reproduce
```

`make reproduce` runs, in order:

| Step | Target | Output |
|---|---|---|
| Create `.venv`, install pinned packages | `setup` | `requirements.txt` |
| Download raw data, verify SHA-256 | `download` | `data/raw/` |
| Read facts from every file, check assumptions | `check` | `results/data_check.json` |
| ECG to R-peaks to RR to epoch features | `features` | `data/cache/` |
| Validate the R-peak detector | `rpeaks` | `results/rpeak_validation.json` |
| Train, choose thresholds on training data, test once on UCDDB | `evaluate` | `results/{sleep_wake,wake_nrem_rem,four_class,apnea}.json`, `results/figures/` |
| Export browser models, results and samples | `web` | `web/data/` |
| Render this README and the write-up from the results | `docs` | `README.md`, `docs/WRITEUP.md` |
| Python/JavaScript parity and unit tests | `parity`, `test` | |

A complete run takes a few hours, most of it downloading. The seed and every
parameter are in [`config/default.toml`](config/default.toml); each results
file records the SHA-256 of the config and of the feature cache it was built
from. The data check currently passes {{v:data_check/n_checks}} of {{v:data_check/n_checks}} checks.

## Configuration

`config/default.toml` holds the seed, the CAP record list, the stage mapping,
the RR artifact rules, the feature windows, model hyperparameters and the
evaluation settings (bootstrap resamples, CI level, inner folds). Change it
and rerun `make features evaluate web docs` to regenerate all outputs.

## Repository layout

```
config/       pipeline configuration (seed, records, rules, models)
somnibeat/    Python package: EDF reading, dataset loaders, R-peaks, RR rules, features, evaluation, report
scripts/      download, data check, feature build, training/evaluation, web export, doc rendering
web/          static demo (index.html, css/, js/, data/, assets/)
tests/        unit tests and Python/JavaScript parity tests
results/      evaluation outputs (JSON and figures)
docs/         evaluation protocol, RR rules, review log, web contract, write-up
```

## Data and licenses

All four datasets are public on PhysioNet under the Open Data Commons
Attribution License v1.0: UCDDB (test), CAP Sleep Database (training,
{{v:sleep_wake/data/train/cap/records}} records), MIT-BIH Polysomnographic Database (training,
{{v:sleep_wake/data/train/slpdb/records}} records from {{v:sleep_wake/data/train/slpdb/subjects}} men) and Apnea-ECG (apnea training,
{{v:apnea/data/train/apnea-ecg/records}} records). Citations, sample attribution and library licenses are in
[`SOURCES.md`](SOURCES.md). The code is released under the MIT License
([`LICENSE`](LICENSE)).

## Not a medical device

Somnibeat has not been validated on home wearables (chest straps, watches,
rings), is not cleared by any regulator, and must not be used to diagnose or
rule out sleep apnea or any other condition.
